        "summary": "Iran's Foreign Minister, Abbas Araghchi, has proposed a deal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and resume talks on its nuclear programme if the US lifts its naval blockade, waives sanctions on Iranian oil sales, and observes a ceasefire that would include Lebanon. The proposal was made at a private gathering on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly in New York. Trita Parsi, executive vice president of the Quincy Institute think tank, suggested that a speedy agreement could help US President Donald Trump ahead of November's midterm elections. There are concerns about whether Iran's hard-liners will accept compromises championed by moderates like President Masoud Pezeshkian.",
