        "summary": "Iran has proposed to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and restart nuclear talks within seven days if the United States agrees to several conditions, including lifting its naval blockade, waiving sanctions on Iranian oil sales, and observing a ceasefire that would include Lebanon. The proposal was made by Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi at a gathering on the sidelines of the U.N. General Assembly. Trita Parsi, executive vice president of the Quincy Institute think tank, suggested that a rapid agreement could help President Donald Trump ahead of November's midterm elections. The offer closely resembles a June agreement, which collapsed after Iran resumed attacks on shipping in the Strait. There is suspicion that Iran could use this agreement to export more oil and reduce economic pressure.",
